  "content": {
    "title": "Who is Amy Madigan dating? What to know about Ed Harris marriage",
    "text": "March 15, 2026, 11:10 a.m. ETAmy Madigan is back in the Oscars race for the first time since 1986, when she earned a Best Supporting Actress nomination for her performance in the Gene Hackman-led drama Twice in a Lifetime.You don't often see a 40-year gap between nominations, but then again you don't see many careers with as much longevity and dependability as Madigan. The 75-year-old showed comedic chops in the John Candy comedy Uncle Buck, infused gravitas into the fantastical baseball film Field of Dreams and played arguably her most iconic role to date in Zach Cregger's Weapons.Madigan plays Aunt Gladys in Weapons, Cregger's wildly successful follow-up to his breakout hit Barbarian. Without divulging spoilers, Aunt Gladys is the wacky yet terrifying antagonist.Throughout the bulk of her career, Madigan has enjoyed a happy marriage with fellow actor Ed Harris. The two met in 1980 when Madigan watched Harris in a play, then married in 1983 and have been together ever since.Madigan and Harris have collaborated on several films together, including 1984's Places in the Heart, 1985's Alamo Bay, 1996's Riders of the Purple Sage, 2000's Pollock, 2007's Gone Baby Gone and 2016's Rules Don't Apply. They have one child together, Lily Dolores Harris, and she has become an actor herself, recently appearing in 2025's Skillhouse.Hollywood royalty indeed.",
    "word_count": 217,
    "extraction_method": "readability"
  },
